  <h1 class="display-4 fw-bold title text-center mb-5">ABOUT ME</h1>
  <img class="coverImage" src= "images/WhatsApp Image .jpg" alt="my picture" width="200px" height="200px" loading="lazy">
        <p class="lead mb-4">Hello! My name is Tobenna Lucky Oguadinma. I am a software developer with a deep passion for reading and for sharing the lessons, ideas, and sparks of inspiration I find in books. For me, reading isn’t just a hobby—it’s a way of learning, growing, and connecting with new perspectives. Every book I finish leaves me with insights worth carrying forward, and this space is where I capture and share them.</p>
        <p class="lead mb-4">This application is designed to help me keep track of the books I’ve read, along with my personal reviews, notes, and reflections. Some entries are short takeaways, others are deeper explorations of themes, but together they form a living record of my reading journey. It’s part journal, part bookshelf, and part creative playground.</p>
        <p class="lead mb-4">I believe books are bridges—between ideas, between people, and between worlds. By sharing my own thoughts here, I hope not only to revisit what I’ve learned but also to invite others into the conversation. Feel free to explore my collection, discover what I’ve been reading lately, and maybe even find something that sparks your curiosity too.</p>

